    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d151">

                <pb facs="0294" n="198" sameAs="frus:frus1872p1/pg198"/>

                <head>No. 151.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Sir Edward Thornton to Mr.
                    Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1872-05-17"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 17,
                        1872</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to your note of the 11th
                    instant, I have the honor to inform you that, in reply to a telegram which I
                    addressed to Earl Granville, his lordship has instructed me to announce to you
                    that Captain Cameron, of the royal artillery, will be appointed Her Britannic
                    Majesty’s commissioner to survey the northwest boundary, and to add that Her
                    Majesty’s government would be glad to learn the views of the Government of the
                    United States as to the commencement of the operations.</p>
                <p>If it should appear to you expedient, orders would be given to Captain Cameron to
                    proceed to Washington for the purpose of making the necessary arrangements in
                    concert with the commissioner who may be appointed on the part of the Government
                    of the United States. I have, &amp;c,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>EDWD. THORNTON.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
